## What to check that the checklist (keyed to the old C1–C9 map) will not tell you

- **Regime split, not a single fix.** This closes the scale-down drain only; the scale-up freeze is
  unchanged and the dev-guide subsection (new, under "Scale-from-zero and zero-replica variants")
  says so explicitly — worth confirming the prose doesn't overclaim.
- **A spec deviation, documented in the status file's C12 section and the commit message:** the plan
  text assumed `throughput` could safely import `pipeline` for the shared `Reason` vocabulary
  (citing `saturation_v2`'s existing alias as precedent). That precedent doesn't transfer —
  `pipeline` imports `internal/config`, and `internal/config`'s own tests import `throughput`, so the
  literal form reopens the same test-binary cycle C10's `resolveKSat` trick routes around (confirmed
  via `go vet ./internal/config/...`, chain printed in the status file). Fixed with the same
  duplicate-constant-plus-drift-guard pattern C10 already established
  (`roleUnmodeledReason` / `TestRoleUnmodeledReasonMatchesPipeline`, mirroring `fallbackKSat` /
  `TestFallbackKSatMatchesConfigDefault`). Worth checking independently that the two literals
  ("role-unmodeled") actually match and that the drift guard would catch it if they didn't.
- **Red-before-fix was verified by mutation** (temporarily disabling the `votesFromRoleSpare` guard,
  confirming exactly three specs fail, restoring), not merely asserted in the commit message.

